A||||7||Eric||Another Autocross||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||05-01-2001||11:49 AM||||There's another autocross this Sunday at the Delphi plant again.  Tech from 8-10am driver's meeting at 10:30am and cars off at 11:00.  This is the driver's school so there is no formal record keeping, just for fun <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If you choose, you can be assigned to an instructor, and he or she will ride with you once and then drive you around once in your car.  It's a good experience because you get to see the lines first hand from an experienced driver at the wheel of your car.  Plus you'll learn about skid control and other handling tricks.  Or you can just run by yourself for the whole day, but I wouldn't suggest it unless you're Roger Garrison and you drive race cars too.<P>So if anyone want to come out and have a good time and learn a lot just go to the Delphi plant with $25 and your car.  Chadman, post directions if you would.  I forgot what road the plant is on.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||05-01-2001||01:09 PM||||Getting there is easy.  On Columbus' west side, take I-270 to the Broad Street exit.  Get off on Broad and head east (toward the city).  When you pass Georgesville Rd, take the first driveway on the right into the plant's side lot.<P>I won't make it this weekend, though.  After the autocross 4/22 and the swap meet 4/27-29, I'd better spend a weekend at home...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||05-01-2001||01:14 PM||||Ahhh seeing more and more posts about Fiero autocrossers just puts a big smile on my face.  Glad to see more Fierophiles racing their cars.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 CSP<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">   <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||05-01-2001||03:13 PM||||Don't know if I'll race this weekend, but I'll be there. I'm consulting a guy in Alabama about tuning my carb for autocrossing, he's been giving me some advice, so hopefully in the next few weeks I'll be back in shape to race. I think I want to replace some more bushings before I start to thrash it around the corners. I also want to install my  oil accumulator. I ran my sump dry about a year ago, resulting in a $1,500 rebuild  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>So I'll be cautious for a little bit...<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||05-01-2001||04:27 PM||||Taijiguy, that would be cool if you could come out to the track if only to watch.  I'd like to see your setup anyway.<P>Chadman, that really sucks that you're not allowed to play again this weekend.  One of these days we have to run against eachother just to see where we stand.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rogergarrison, you should try to make it out too so atleast I won't be the only Fiero type car on the lot this Sunday.  I'd also like to see the Ferrari in action.  I'm going to bring doughnuts out to try and lure the Fieros to the autocross.<P>Greg Piet, people don't realize how much fun this sport is.  For instance, Chadman just couldn't wipe the smile off his face at the last race.  It's really cool to see people getting excited about racing their cars.  And I think I'll disclose all my engine mods to the officials if only becuase everyone else here, with the exception of Chadman, will be running E mod too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||05-01-2001||04:31 PM||||What qualifies as E Mod? I used to race my 73 Cutlass (don't laugh, that was one badassed autocrosser..I even beat a guy who trailered in a Vette) The Cutlass was lowered, and had a built 350, and was always put in "B Stock Prepared"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||05-01-2001||04:41 PM||||"B Stock Prepared??""<P>B Street prepared I think is what you mean<BR>Corvettes and such dominate the land of BSP for the most part<P>E mod is basically the wildest cars out there. Steve Tamandili in a Fiero use to win it a lot , not sure if he did last year. His car just looked like a Fiero , it ran a Aluminum Buick v8  , I believe a hewland trans Axle or a ZF. The car's only relation to a Fiero were the body panels , From what I have heard it was built around some sort of Formula car , I'm not sure if it still is , but the one pic I have of it , the driver is mid mounted...<P><BR>E mod is filled with light cars with big power. MG midgets with Wankel motors , The lighter and small the better...not a place For a Fiero to play. No matter what engine conversion or suspension you have.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000007||Taijiguy||05-01-2001||04:48 PM||||You're right, street prepared. I just looked at the time sheets. Been a long time since I ran that car.<BR>Ironically, I stomped my friends brother in his 84 Rustang, and absolutely crushed some modified cars, including a Tygr, the Vette-(B/P), and a Shelby (also B/P)<BR>I got beat up by an MR2 though, how humiliating...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
